# Income date range

Each `IncomeSource` can optionally set inclusive `startYear` / `endYear`. Omit
both and the source runs for the whole projection.

## Amount vs growth

The entered monthly amount is what you receive **in the start year**. Growth
compounds only after that. If `startYear` is omitted, the first projection year
is the start. `growthDelayYears` (spreadsheet quirk) is extra flat years after
that start, not after year 0 of the plan.

This used to grow from year 0 even while the source was inactive, so a Social
Security line that started later was already inflated when it kicked in. Don't
put that back.

`incomeMonthlyForYear` in `household.ts` is the single source. `project.ts`,
`convertible.ts`, and `depleteByRmd.ts` must call it; don't re-derive grown
amounts from `yearIndex`.

## Pension payout (survivorship)

Pension kinds (`pension`, `militaryPension`) carry `pensionPayout`:
`lifeOnly` (stops when the owner passes) or `survivor` (keeps paying the
surviving spouse for life). Missing means life only; read it through
`pensionPayout()` in `household.ts`, which returns undefined for non-pensions.
`migrateHousehold` drops it from non-pensions and bad values, and the editor
clears it when the type changes away from a pension.

The choice only matters in the Survivorship analysis (see the analyses
feature guide), where a spouse's death is modeled.

## Disability insurance

`disabilityInsurance` incomes add `disabilityWaitingDays` (30 / 60 / 90 /
180, default 90) and `disabilityCoverage` (`full`, default, or `partial`,
which pays half). Read them through `disabilityWaitingDays()` /
`disabilityCoverage()`, which return undefined for other kinds.
`startYear` / `endYear` are the benefit period (the editor calls it that).
`incomeMonthlyForYear` applies both: the wait runs from January 1 of the
first benefit year (30 days = one month), so a 90-day wait pays 9 of 12
months that year. New disability lines default to tax free (individual
policy); employer-paid plans switch to taxable. The benefit stops when its
owner passes (Survivorship). `migrateHousehold` strips the fields from
other kinds and drops bad values.
